        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "699be91e-0245-5562-8dba-44390aa2d349",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Nikolaschka, White Russian\n- Ingredients: cognac brandy, lemon disk, coffee powder, powdered sugar, vodka, coffee liqueur, Kahlúa, Tia Maria, cream, milk, ice\n- Glassware: brandy snifter, Old Fashioned glass\n\nFacts:\n- The Nikolaschka is prepared by pouring cognac brandy into a brandy snifter and placing a lemon disk on top of the glass.\n- The Nikolaschka is then finished by covering half of the lemon disk with coffee powder and the other half with powdered sugar before serving.\n- A White Russian is a cocktail made with vodka, coffee liqueur such as Kahlúa or Tia Maria, and cream, and it is served with ice in an Old Fashioned glass.\n- A White Russian is often made with milk as an alternative to cream.",
